#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124225 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124659 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1bc2396-f949-57a0-be50-d5606abe3372" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d2479726-b486-5bc2-864f-98a3659d81d5" :question/math-academy-id "e-1470" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x)=x^2+4x+6$?" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in standard form,\n\n$$\ny = ax^2+bx+c\n$$\n\nwith $a=1>0$, $b=4$, and $c=6$.\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is positive, the parabola opens upward. Consequently, there is no maximum output, and the vertex corresponds to the minimum output.\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is given by\n\n$$\nx= -\\dfrac{b}{2a} = -\\dfrac{4}{2 \\cdot 1} = -2\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $x=-2$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= x^{2} + 4x + 6 \\\\\n&= (-2)^{2} + 4(-2) + 6 \\\\\n&= 4 - 8 + 6 \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-2,2)$, and the range of the function is $[2,\\infty)$.\n\n![](images/41/41b7219793120c0e37b3d910ef6a8f3754c1d9f27b784f937381743d7b7a85df.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124226 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0d6e0e-bf61-5fe9-bf8a-ab15c5846e11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Factored Form"}] :question/id #uuid "f69335f5-b5df-5053-8127-a7489c711b5f" :question/math-academy-id "e-1472" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) = -\\dfrac{1}{2}(x+3)(x-1)$?" :question/worked-solution "The given parabola is written in factored form,\n\n$$\ny = a(x-x_1)(x-x_2)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\na = -\\dfrac{1}{2} < 0\n$$\n\nBecause the leading coefficient is negative, the parabola opens downward. Consequently, there is no minimum output, and the vertex corresponds to the maximum output.\n\nThe two roots of the parabola are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=1$, and we can find the $x$-coordinate of the vertex by taking the average of the roots:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= \\frac{x_{1} + x_{2}}{2} = \\frac{-3 + 1}{2} =-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute $x=-1$ back into the function to find the $y$-value of the vertex:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= -\\frac{1}{2}(x + 3)(x - 1) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}(-1 + 3)(-1 - 1) \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 2 \\cdot (-2) \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertex is $(-1,2)$, and the range of the function is $(-\\infty,2]$.\n\n![](images/2f/2f949680675dd0b0347adc154b8be6ce301ddb2f5b1b9ab0c077a5c00f81568f.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124391 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124583 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "713fb1a0-5d7b-5cde-aafe-de5887086e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain of a Quadratic Function"}] :question/id #uuid "59873e3c-c8ba-5844-874a-01cf298b361d" :question/math-academy-id "e-7992" :question/problem "What is the domain of the function $g(x)=\\dfrac{4}{3}x^2+5x -12$?" :question/worked-solution "A quadratic function is defined for all real numbers.\n\nTherefore, the domain of $g(x)$ is $x\\in(-\\infty,\\infty)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124393 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124584 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "56d457de-8511-5870-98e3-b81e72e60585" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Vertex Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d6a69eb7-e598-51e8-92e9-fad42b3c0978" :question/math-academy-id "e-8027" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) = (x+3)^2-2$?" :question/worked-solution "The parabola is written in vertex form,\n\n$$\ny = a(x-h)^2 + k\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the leading coefficient and $(h,k)$ is the vertex.\n\n- Since $h=-3$ and $k=-2$, the vertex is $(-3,-2)$.\n- Since $a=1>0$, the parabola opens upwards.\n\nBecause the parabola opens upwards, the vertex corresponds to the minimum output, while there is no maximum output.\n\nTherefore, the range is $[-2,\\infty)$.\n\nThe corresponding diagram is shown below.\n\n![](images/57/579eef7814c2b51c44cded6fb2dc64e36d1106d359864e1e7ec7354511f80681.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124875 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124660 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fb0d6e0e-bf61-5fe9-bf8a-ab15c5846e11" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of a Parabola Given in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "936b7e37-8c5e-5979-8bce-f7d294f4f7be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞, \\frac{4}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121851} {:answer/id #uuid "9a5b3be5-7ef9-55ed-acaf-bfe10de6dfd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞,-\\frac{4}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121852} {:answer/id #uuid "a378cdb8-0895-50ec-8260-fae1a30ae7e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\frac{4}{3}, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121853} {:answer/id #uuid "d08aabc1-13cc-5a3d-b417-ead743280afa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[- \\frac{4}{3}, ∞)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121854} {:answer/id #uuid "5ca63e9f-28bb-5e4e-a253-eb11d198b66a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- ∞, \\frac{1}{3}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121855}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8f8e4aed-0ad7-583b-bf1d-eb2a74efae0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121850}] :question/id #uuid "7bfd7586-e0f5-50a2-a9b8-3d8eb173ed99" :question/math-academy-id "q-35155" :question/problem "What is the range of the function $f(x) =-\\frac{1}{3}(x + 2)(x - 2)$?"}]}
